@startuml Assignment Sequence

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor DarkBlue
    ActorBorderColor DarkBlue
    LifeLineBorderColor DarkBlue
    ParticipantBackgroundColor LightBlue
    ParticipantBorderColor DarkBlue
}

title User Assignment Flow (Idempotent)

actor Client
participant "FastAPI" as API
participant "Auth" as Auth
participant "Cache" as Cache
participant "Assignment\nService" as Service
database "SQLite" as DB

== First Request ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments/{id}/assignment/{user_id}\n[Authorization: Bearer token]
API -> Auth : Validate token
Auth --> API : Token valid

API -> Cache : Check cache\nkey: "assignment:{id}:{user_id}"
Cache --> API : Cache miss

API -> Service : Get or create assignment
Service -> DB : Query existing assignment
DB --> Service : Not found

Service -> DB : Query variants for experiment
DB --> Service : Variants list

Service -> Service : Calculate weighted\nrandom selection

Service -> DB : INSERT assignment
DB --> Service : Assignment created

Service -> Cache : Store in cache (TTL: 5min)
Cache --> Service : Cached

Service --> API : AssignmentResponse
API --> Client : 200 OK\n{"variant_name": "Control", ...}

== Subsequent Request (Same User) ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments/{id}/assignment/{user_id}\n[Authorization: Bearer token]
API -> Auth : Validate token
Auth --> API : Token valid

API -> Cache : Check cache\nkey: "assignment:{id}:{user_id}"
Cache --> API : Cache hit!

API --> Client : 200 OK\n{"variant_name": "Control", ...}\n(Same assignment - Idempotent)

note right of Cache
  Cache ensures fast
  subsequent requests
  and guarantees
  idempotency
end note

@enduml
